From: Veron
Subject: [PATCH] aarch64: three macros encode x16 as x8 in the Rn field

    DEFINE add_x0,x16,x0 0020008b        ->  ADD x0, x0, x0, LSL #8

Not a missing macro -- a WRONG one. It assembles, it links, it runs, and it is
used 315 times in one compile of libtcc.c. Every one computed garbage.

All three have the same typo. Rn=16 needs bits 5-9 set to 0b10000, which is
0x200; they carry 0x100, which is Rn=8.

    add_x0,x16,x0      0020008b   ADD x0, x0, x0, LSL #8   -> 0002008b
    add_x18,x16,x18    1201128b   ADD x18, x8, x18         -> 1202128b
    sub_x18,x16,x18    120112cb   SUB x18, x8, x18         -> 120212cb

HOW IT PRESENTED. "Struct assignment is broken on aarch64 and only aarch64" --
a sentence that sends you looking at alignment. It is the SOURCE-POINTER
ADVANCE in the struct copy, so the size of the struct decided everything:

    8-byte struct    one chunk, the advance is never used again    works
    16-byte struct   second chunk reads from 8 + (8 << 8) = 2056   SIGSEGV

Case 05 has been red on aarch64 since it was written and this is why. Case 46
too. Both pass with this patch; the emitted copy loop was correct all along
and was assembling into something else.

vocabulary.sh CANNOT FIND THIS. It asks whether every macro micro-c can emit
exists for the target, and all three do exist. The question it cannot ask is
whether the macro that exists is correct. tools/verify_defs.py asks that one:
for register-to-register forms the encoding is fully determined by the name,
so the two can be compared by machine. It reports these three and nothing else
across 109 checked macros.

Verified on aarch64 under qemu: the whole case suite goes from 41 pass 3 fail
to 43 pass 1 fail, with only 16-switch-wide left.

diff --git a/aarch64/aarch64_defs.M1 b/aarch64/aarch64_defs.M1
index 1d83aea..8d22ed0 100644
--- a/aarch64/aarch64_defs.M1
+++ b/aarch64/aarch64_defs.M1
@@ -845,7 +845,7 @@ DEFINE add_x0,x14,x0 c001008b
 DEFINE ADD_X0_X15_X0 e001008b ; add x0, x15, x0
 DEFINE add_x0,x15,x0 e001008b
 DEFINE ADD_X0_X16_X0 0020008b ; add x0, x16, x0
-DEFINE add_x0,x16,x0 0020008b
+DEFINE add_x0,x16,x0 0002008b
 DEFINE ADD_X0_BP_X0 2002008b
 DEFINE add_x0,x17,x0 2002008b
 DEFINE ADD_X1_SP_8 41220091
@@ -861,7 +861,7 @@ DEFINE add_x18,x14,x18 d201128b
 DEFINE ADD_SP_X15_SP f201128b ; add x18, x15, x18
 DEFINE add_x18,x15,x18 f201128b
 DEFINE ADD_SP_X16_SP 1201128b ; add x18, x16, x18
-DEFINE add_x18,x16,x18 1201128b
+DEFINE add_x18,x16,x18 1202128b
 DEFINE add_x1,x1,x0 2100008b
 DEFINE add_x1,x1,x5 2100058b
 DEFINE add_x1,x1,x3 2100038b
@@ -908,7 +908,7 @@ DEFINE sub_x18,x14,x18 d20112cb
 DEFINE SUB_SP_X15_SP f20112cb ; sub x18, x15, x18
 DEFINE sub_x18,x15,x18 f20112cb
 DEFINE SUB_SP_X16_SP 120112cb ; sub x18, x16, x18
-DEFINE sub_x18,x16,x18 120112cb
+DEFINE sub_x18,x16,x18 120212cb
 DEFINE SUB_SP_SP_X14 52020ecb ; sub x18, x18, x14
 DEFINE sub_x18,x18,x14 52020ecb
 DEFINE SUB_SP_SP_X15 52020fcb ; sub x18, x18, x15
